From: ROG5 Linux contributors <klimovich008@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: asus-rog5-ams678: send brightness in LP mode

The backlight callback cleared MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM and sent 0x51 in HS
mode. On the phone the panel ignores that write: the DBV stays at the
value last written in LP mode, which is 0 from enable(), so the screen
stays black at any brightness. Measured on 2026-09-23 (production
display trials d4 and d5) with the phone's input current as a light
meter: a white frame drew the same idle current after HS writes of 1 or
1023, but the USB input limit plus battery current after an LP write of
1023, and idle again after an LP write of 1 or 0. The stock init
sequence is unchanged and works once the DBV arrives in LP mode.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-asus-rog5-ams678.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-asus-rog5-ams678.c
@@ -387,7 +387,11 @@
 		return -EPERM;
 	}
 	mode_flags = dsi->mode_flags;
-	dsi->mode_flags &= ~MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
+	/*
+	 * The panel ignores 0x51 sent in HS mode: the DBV stays at the value
+	 * last written in LP mode (0 from enable), so the screen stays dark.
+	 */
+	dsi->mode_flags |= MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
 	/* Vendor inverted-DBV handling sends the high byte first. */
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(dsi, brightness);
